      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Align config watermark opacity clamp",
        "body": "Fixes #11\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAlign config import handling for `watermarkOpacity` with the Settings UI range.\r\n\r\nThe Settings UI allows watermark opacity up to `0.5`, but `ConfigProposal` previously clamped imported deep-link values to `0.3`. That meant a shared config link with a valid value like `0.45` would silently import as `0.3`.\r\n\r\nThis updates the import clamp to `0...0.5` and adds focused regression coverage for preserving values inside the Settings UI range.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n- `swift build`\r\n\r\nFocused behavior proof:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF import-0.45=0.45\r\nPROOF import-1.0-clamped=0.5\r\nPROOF import-negative-clamped=0.0\r\n```",
        "branch": "fix/issue-11-config-opacity-clamp",
